# Awesome Hacking (Cursor Rule)

Use the **awesome-hacking** skill (`skills/awesome-hacking/SKILL.md`, `.agents/skills/awesome-hacking/SKILL.md`) when the user wants curated security lists (Android, AppSec, Bug Bounty, AI Security, Cryptography, Forensics, Payloads, Reverse Engineering, Web Security, etc.) for owner-authorized auditing.

## Core behavior
- Awesome Hacking (hack-with-github/awesome-hacking) is a collection of various awesome lists for hackers, pentesters, and security researchers.
- Only apply techniques/tools against targets the user owns or has explicit, written authorization to test.
- No third-party targets; never attack systems outside authorized scope.
- CC0-1.0 licensed; referenced externally only — no content copied into REA_Skill (MIT).
- Pair with REA skills (`rea-binary-disassembly`, `offensive-api-security`, `offensive-fuzzing`, `offensive-cloud`, `offensive-mobile`).